{"id": "7651", "revid": "2164467", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=7651", "title": "Clara", "text": "Clara is a town in County Offaly in the midlands of Ireland. It's on the main Dublin-Galway railway and has become a commuter town for the capital, with a population of 3400 in 2022. Its main sight, 2 km south, is the wetland of Clara Bog. \nGet in.\nBy road from Dublin follow M6 to junction 5. From there N52 heads south to Tullamore, but you need to circle north through Kilbeggan to get onto R436 to Clara.\nTrains from Dublin Heuston run every couple of hours, taking an hour to Clara via Portarlington and Tullamore. They continue west to Athlone then branch either to Athenry and Galway or to Roscommon, Castlebar and Westport. See Irish Rail for times, fares and online tickets. \n is south side of town. \nBus \u00c9ireann 73 traverses the country from Waterford via Thomastown, Kilkenny, Carlow, Stradbally, Portlaoise and Tullamore to Clara and Athlone. There are two M-Sa; the one Sunday bus continues north to Ballymahon and Longford. \nLocal Link buses are: \n - Bus 815 five times a day from Athlone to Clara, Tubber, Moate and Tullamore. \n - Bus 840 from Banagher to Ballycumber, Clara, Ballinamere and Tullamore, with 6 M-F and 4 Sa Su. \n - Bus 850 connects with the 840 at Banagher. It runs six times a day from Athlone to Clonmacnoise, Shannonbridge, Banagher, Birr and Roscrea. On Sunday it continues to Thurles.\n \"Evil men \u2013 demons in human form (...) lure girls from the town to go for motor drives into the country, and you know what happens - it is not for the benefit of the motor drive. It is for something infinitely worse.\" \u2014 sermon circa 1930 \nGet around.\nSo you'd better walk or cycle.\nEat.\nStrung along the main road are Rose Garden, Macari's takeaway, Mill Bar, Super Kebab, Jel's Kitchen, Yummy House and Mario's.\nDrink.\nAlong on the main road are Nigel's Place, Dessi Dolan's and Christy Cowen's.\nSee Tullamore for the Tullamore Dew and Kilbeggan distilleries. Both offer tours.\nConnect.\nAs of June 2026, Clara and its approach roads have 4G from Eir and Three, and 5G from Vodafone."}
