{"id": "7705", "revid": "235382", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=7705", "title": "Clayton (New Mexico)", "text": "Clayton is a small town in extreme northeastern New Mexico, in the United States. The historic Santa Fe Trail passed near here."}
{"id": "7707", "revid": "70028", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=7707", "title": "Clearlake", "text": "Clearlake is a city in Lake County inland in the North Coast region of California. It is located at the southern end of Clear Lake, which is more than 1.5 million years old.\nGet in.\nBy bus.\nLake Transit offers service from several nearby towns, including Calistoga, where you can make connections from the Bay Area, and Ukiah, where you can make connections from Mendocino."}
