{"id": "7709", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=7709", "title": "Clear Lake (Iowa)", "text": "Clear Lake is a city in North Central Iowa. \nUnderstand.\nIt is most famous as the place \"the music died\" because shortly after leaving a concert at the Surf Ballroom in 1959, a small plane carrying rock artists Buddy Holly, Richie Valens, and J.P. \"The Big Bopper\" Richardson crashed in a corn field just outside town.\nGet in.\nLocated at the junction of Interstate 35 and U.S. Highway 18."}
